  "limitations": [
    "The background loop is enabled only when Control has a valid transparent trust root and verified driver registry; these checks use synthetic releases and fake executors rather than a real signed provider installation.",
    "The stable read transaction and keyset pagination prevent a delayed first page from starving later ready work, but they can scan every nonterminal workflow; very large catalogs still need indexed eligibility, load measurements, and scan-duration telemetry.",
    "Driver-selection failures now persist a typed Catalog error code, a bounded message, failure count, exact child identity, and exponential retry time. Those diagnostics are not yet exposed through the public API, CLI, Web console, or production metrics.",
    "The pass validates live-claim exclusion and stale selector/result race fences, but it does not submit a deployment to a real provider account or prove multi-Control-instance behavior against a shared production database.",
    "The process-level 15-second drain is tested structurally and by existing server drain tests; this exact portability slice does not kill a real long-running provider CLI during shutdown on every host.",
    "The registry and dispatcher still have no complete public vault, release, target, provider-deployment, and operation management surface in this evidence.",
    "The release, keys, roots, transparency proof, witness signatures, and provider process fixtures remain synthetic, and no backend is certified against Edge Canon by these checks.",
